@lang en
IMPORT `pc-travel-general`

-- Pacific Cross Vietnam, Travel Insurance Policy: CLAIMS PROCEDURE (English src:999-1072,
-- Vietnamese src:2127-2203). The insurer's own deadline to assess and pay is not stated in
-- either text (Law on Insurance Business Art. 31, Law line 718-724, supplies 15 days from a
-- complete dossier: fork LAW-PAY, not encoded).
--
-- Days are calendar days (fork F-DAYS). The regulative rules count on a clock whose unit is
-- one day and whose zero is the day the period starts to run.

§ `Claims procedure`
-- src:999 | CLAIMS PROCEDURE
-- src:2127 | THỦ TỤC YÊU CẦU BỒI THƯỜNG

§§ `CP 1 — notice of a claim within 30 days`
-- src:1003 | 1. Notice of any claim must be given to the Company within 30
-- src:1004 | days of the expiry of this Policy or the date of finishing the trip
-- src:1005 | covered by this Policy (applicable to Annual Travel), and in the
-- src:1006 | instance of a claim under the “Personal Liability” section of this
-- src:2128 | 1. Phải nộp thông báo yêu cầu bồi thường cho Công ty trong vòng
-- src:2129 | 30 ngày kể từ ngày kết thúc Hợp đồng bảo hiểm này hoặc kể
-- src:2130 | từ ngày kết thúc chuyến đi được bảo hiểm bởi Hợp đồng bảo
-- src:2131 | hiểm này (áp dụng đối với bảo hiểm du lịch Annual Travel),
-- "within 30 days of the expiry of this Policy or the date of finishing the trip covered by
-- this Policy (applicable to Annual Travel)": from the last day of the Period of Insurance, or
-- for Annual Travel from the day the trip finished.
GIVEN c IS A `The case`
      d IS A `The dates of a claim`
GIVETH A DATE
`CP 1 — the last day to give notice of the claim` c d MEANS
    IF   c's `certificate`'s `product` EQUALS `Annual Travel`
    THEN d's `date the trip covered by this Policy finished` PLUS 30
    ELSE c's `certificate`'s `last day of the Period of Insurance` PLUS 30

GIVEN c IS A `The case`
      d IS A `The dates of a claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CP 1 — notice of the claim was given in time` c d MEANS
    CONSIDER d's `date notice of the claim was given`
    WHEN NOTHING     THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST given  THEN given AT MOST `CP 1 — the last day to give notice of the claim` c d

-- The notice duty as a regulative rule, its clock starting at the expiry (or the end of the
-- trip). CP 1 states no consequence; clause 1 makes observance a condition precedent to any
-- liability, and the breach says so. LAW: Art. 46(2) (Law line 928-931) bars a reduction for
-- late notice where the contract names no sanction for it (fork LAW-NOTICE).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to the Policy` `An act under the Policy`
`CP 1 — the duty to give notice of a claim` MEANS
    PARTY  `the Insured Person`
    MUST   `give notice of the claim`
    WITHIN 30
    LEST   BREACH BY `the Insured Person` BECAUSE "CP 1: notice of the claim was not given within 30 days of the expiry of the Policy (or of the end of the trip, for Annual Travel); clause 1 makes compliance a condition precedent to liability"

§§ `CP 1 — Personal Liability: written notice within 15 days of the incident`
-- src:1006 | instance of a claim under the “Personal Liability” section of this
-- src:1007 | Policy such notice must be given in writing as soon as possible
-- src:1008 | and in any event not later than 15 days after the incident which
-- src:1009 | may give rise to such a claim. The Company shall not accept
-- src:2131 | hiểm này (áp dụng đối với bảo hiểm du lịch Annual Travel),
-- src:2132 | và trong trường hợp yêu cầu bồi thường theo mục “Trách
-- src:2133 | nhiệm cá nhân” của Hợp đồng bảo hiểm này thì thông báo đó
-- src:2134 | phải được gửi bằng văn bản càng sớm càng tốt và không được
-- src:2135 | muộn hơn 15 ngày kể từ khi xảy ra sự cố. Công ty sẽ không
-- "as soon as possible and in any event not later than 15 days after the incident": the
-- encoding tests the outer limit; "as soon as possible" has no measure a rule can apply.
GIVEN d IS A `The dates of a claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `CP 1 — written notice of a Personal Liability claim was given in time` d IF
        d's `notice given in writing`
    AND `within 15 days` (d's `date notice of the claim was given`)
    WHERE
        `within 15 days` m MEANS
            CONSIDER m
            WHEN NOTHING    THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST given THEN given AT MOST (d's `date of the incident` PLUS 15)

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to the Policy` `An act under the Policy`
`CP 1 — the duty to give written notice of a possible Personal Liability claim` MEANS
    PARTY  `the Insured Person`
    MUST   `give written notice of a possible Personal Liability claim`
    WITHIN 15
    LEST   BREACH BY `the Insured Person` BECAUSE "CP 1: no written notice of the Personal Liability claim within 15 days after the incident"

§§ `CP 1 — further information within 60 days of a written request`
-- src:1009 | may give rise to such a claim. The Company shall not accept
-- src:1010 | liability for any claim if the required information is not received
-- src:1011 | within 60 days from the issue date of any written request from
-- src:1012 | the Company requesting such further information, and the
-- src:1013 | claim is thereafter deemed to be abandoned. All claims shall
-- src:2135 | muộn hơn 15 ngày kể từ khi xảy ra sự cố. Công ty sẽ không
-- src:2136 | chấp nhận trách nhiệm đối với bất kỳ yêu cầu bồi thường nào
-- src:2137 | mà Công ty không nhận được thông tin yêu cầu trong vòng 60
-- src:2138 | ngày kể từ ngày Công ty có văn bản yêu cầu cung cấp thêm
-- src:2139 | thông tin đó, và sau đó yêu cầu bồi thường được xem như bị
-- src:2140 | từ bỏ. Tất cả các yêu cầu bồi thường phải được kèm theo cùng
GIVEN d       IS A `The dates of a claim`
      `as at` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CP 1 — the claim is deemed abandoned for want of information, as at` d `as at` MEANS
    CONSIDER d's `date of the Company's written request for further information`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST requested THEN
        CONSIDER d's `date the required information was received`
        WHEN NOTHING        THEN `as at` GREATER THAN (requested PLUS 60)
        WHEN JUST received  THEN received GREATER THAN (requested PLUS 60)

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to the Policy` `An act under the Policy`
`CP 1 — the duty to provide the further information requested` MEANS
    PARTY  `the Insured Person`
    MUST   `provide the further information requested`
    WITHIN 60
    LEST   BREACH BY `the Insured Person` BECAUSE "CP 1: the required information was not received within 60 days from the issue date of the Company's written request; the claim is deemed abandoned"

§§ `CP 1 — proof satisfactory to the Company, at the Insured Person's expense`
-- src:1013 | claim is thereafter deemed to be abandoned. All claims shall
-- src:1014 | be made together with proof satisfactory to the Company in
-- src:1015 | the case of Death, Illness, Disability, Injury or loss for which a
-- src:1016 | claim is made hereunder and shall be rendered on demand at
-- src:1017 | the Insured Person’s own expense.
-- src:2140 | từ bỏ. Tất cả các yêu cầu bồi thường phải được kèm theo cùng
-- src:2141 | với bằng chứng thỏa đáng trong trường hợp bị tử vong, Ốm
-- src:2142 | đau, bệnh tật, Thương tích hoặc tổn thất và phải được nộp cho
-- src:2143 | Công ty theo yêu cầu với chi phí do Người được bảo hiểm chịu.
-- English: "proof satisfactory to the Company"; Vietnamese "bằng chứng thỏa đáng" (adequate
-- proof), without "to the Company" (VN-F10). A judgement with no criteria; inert as a rule.

§§ `CP 2 — the documents each section's claim needs`
